Changelog - Discord Recruitment Bot
Fixed Issues
🐛 Critical Bug: Users couldn't see their own threads
Problem: Private threads were created but the requesting user wasn't added as a member
Fix: Added await thread.add_user(interaction.user) in both /recruit and /officer commands
Impact: Users can now actually see and participate in the threads they create

🐛 Role members not automatically added to threads
Problem: Only role mentions were sent, but role members couldn't see private threads
Fix: Now loops through all members with the appropriate role and adds them to the thread
Lines affected: 104-109 (recruit), 168-173 (officer)
  
🔍 Case-sensitive duplicate thread detection
Problem: Users could create multiple threads like "Recruit-John" and "recruit-john"
Fix: Changed to case-insensitive comparison using .lower()
Lines affected: 79, 149
  
🛡️ Unreliable role permission checking
Problem: role in user.roles could fail silently
Fix: Changed to any(role.id == ROLE_ID for role in user.roles) for more reliable ID-based checking
Lines affected: 204, 232
  
📬 Reminder command sent DMs instead of posting in channel
Problem: Reminders would DM the user, losing context of which thread it was about
Fix: Now posts reminder in the same channel/thread where it was set, with DM as fallback
Lines affected: 242-252
  
🛡️ Missing error handling for thread creation
Problem: Thread creation could fail (permissions, rate limits) without graceful handling
Fix: Wrapped thread creation in try-except blocks with user-friendly error messages
Lines affected: 93-133, 157-188
  
📝 Reminder command loses context on channel deletion
Problem: If channel/thread was deleted before reminder fired, bot would crash
Fix: Added fallback to DM user if channel is no longer accessible
Lines affected: 247-252
  
Remaining Limitations
⚠️ Reminder persistence: Reminders won't survive a bot restart (requires database)
⚠️ No auto-cleanup: Old archived threads aren't automatically deleted
⚠️ Assumes "bot-logs" channel exists: Logging will silently fail if channel doesn't exist

Total lines modified: ~70 lines across 8 different sections
